---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { repository } from "../content/product";
---
<Page title="UI Torture Lab" description="Stress text on your own web interface. Investigate measured layout regressions, Restore, and copy the Evidence as Markdown." home>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="product-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">A field tool for frontend developers · Chrome desktop</p>
    <h1 id="product-title">UI Torture Lab</h1>
    <p class="promise">Stress text.<br />Investigate what breaks.</p>
    <p>Apply a deterministic text Scenario to an interface you own or can modify. Inspect new or measurably worsened layout regressions, Restore, and copy the Evidence as Markdown.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/install/">Installation &amp; release status</a><a href="/docs/">Read the workflow</a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 / Evidence before interpretation</p>
    <h2 id="evidence-title">A measured change.<br />A place to investigate.</h2>
    <div class="columns">
      <figure class="specimen">
        <p class="eyebrow">Baseline / synthetic example</p><div class="sample">Checkout</div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Long Text / synthetic example</p><div class="sample" aria-label="Expanded checkout text clipped by its boundary">Checkout Checkout Checkout</div>
        <figcaption>Illustration only. A Text Clipping Finding requires comparable geometry on the same connected element before and after Mutation.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div><h3>Read before and after</h3><p class="evidence">Subject: clipping boundary<br />Baseline: visible text<br />Mutated: a newly hidden range<br />Measured Delta: CSS pixels<br />Possible Cause: a hypothesis</p><p>Findings describe supported geometric regressions. They carry no severity, quality score, or accessibility verdict.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">02 / One Scenario at a time</p><h2 id="workflow-title">Open. Stress. Inspect. Restore.</h2>
    <ol class="steps"><li>Open your interface in Google Chrome desktop stable and click the extension toolbar action.</li><li>Choose one Scenario. The Run captures a Baseline, applies temporary Mutations, and compares supported Evidence.</li><li>Inspect a Finding Subject or Primary Contributor. Investigate the relevant HTML and CSS in your own tools.</li><li>Use explicit Restore, then Copy Report as Markdown. Reload if cleanup cannot be verified.</li></ol>
    <p><a href="/docs/">Understand coverage, inconclusive results, and safe Restore →</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 / Current build</p><h2 id="capabilities-title">Three Scenarios.<br />Three geometric Detectors.</h2>
    <div class="columns"><div><h3>Scenarios</h3><dl><dt><strong>Long Text</strong></dt><dd>Repeats eligible text three times while preserving target identity.</dd><dt><strong>Unbreakable Text</strong></dt><dd>Appends one fixed 64-character token without adding wrapping opportunities.</dd><dt><strong>Large Text</strong></dt><dd>Doubles stable computed font sizes on eligible Text Scaling Targets.</dd></dl></div><div><h3>Detectors</h3><dl><dt><strong>Text Clipping</strong></dt><dd>New or worsened text hidden by a proven clipping boundary.</dd><dt><strong>Horizontal Containment Overflow</strong></dt><dd>New or worsened excess beyond a proven containing boundary.</dd><dt><strong>Viewport Overflow</strong></dt><dd>New or worsened page-level horizontal extent with a stable contributor.</dd></dl></div></div>
    <p>The Official Distribution’s MVP is free, needs no account, and has no gated features. <a href="/license/">Read the distribution contract.</a></p>
    <p>No Findings does not establish that the page has no layout problems. <a href="/scope/">Read the Supported Scope.</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="home-section"><h2>Know the boundary before you install.</h2><p>Chrome desktop stable, Manifest V3, top-level light-DOM HTML over HTTP or HTTPS. Localhost is supported. Read the usage guide before changing routes or navigating during a Run.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/install/">Check installation status</a><a href={repository}>Inspect the public source</a></div></section>
</Page>
